        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          Test of resistance to different agents with treatment of radiation, or hydrogen peroxide or acid after growth under normal gravity (NG) and LSMMG. For survival data LHM4 strain was used as this is a derivative of strain 1218R. A plasmid is incorporated into the genome that encodes red fluorescent protein and kanamycin resistance. Bacteria were grown and treated according to Abshire et al NOJ Microgravity  (2016) 2, 16038; doi:10.1038/npjmgrav.2016.38. 
<p>
LHM4 were removed from the HARV and the OD600 measured in a sample after disaggregation. Bacteria were in exponential phase (OD600 0.09-0.2). For radiation and hydrogen peroxide (H2O2) studies, bacteria were centrifuged and washed in PBS containing 0.2% Tween 80 (Tw-PBS) , before resuspension at OD600 ~0.2 in Tw-PBS. Two samples (200 µl in a sealed tube) were prepared for each time point or dose. One sample was treated (1-4 hours) with 5 mM H2O2 at 30°C or with ? radiation (100-400 Gy) at room temperature. The second sample was not treated and was used as the control to determine the CFU/ ml at zero treatment at the time point. A similar method was used to treat the bacteria with acid. The bacteria were centrifuged and resuspended at OD600 ~0.2 in growth medium (control) or growth medium at pH 3.5. 1 M citric acid was added to the medium to reach pH 3.5. Once the bacteria were resuspended, the pH was checked using pH paper. The control and acid-treated samples were incubated at 30°C for 1-4 hours. After all treatment regimens, bacteria were disaggregated and diluted as described above and grown on three plates containing solid medium. Bacteria were incubated at 30°C for 7-10 days and the CFU/ ml calculated for each control and treated sample. Survival was calculated by:% Survival = Avg CFU/ ml of treated culture x 100, Avg CFU/ ml of control culture
<p>
The survival data were compared by calculating the area under the curve for each data set using the Trapezoidal Rule, and the Student T test was used to compare the values. These statistical analyses were performed using SAS 9.4 (SAS Inc. Gary, NC).
<p>
Time period of collection range from February 3, 2014 to February 17, 2015.
        </div>

